# Git guesses text vs binary, and it guessed wrong on the manual: it warned
# that LF would become CRLF "next time Git touches it", which for a PDF means
# a checkout on a fresh clone produces a corrupt file. Say so explicitly.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.xlsx  binary

# Normalise everything else to LF in the repository, whatever the checkout
# does locally — this project is developed on Windows and deployed on Linux.
* text=auto
